-- ... or to both
#ASSERT `form 6.2 if the person commits an offence under subsection 145(3), the Form states that` TRUE `forms 6 to 11.1 the person may be liable to both a fine and imprisonment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a consequence the sentence does not name: not covered
#ASSERT `form 6.2 if the person commits an offence under subsection 145(3), the Form states that` TRUE `forms 6 to 11.1 another consequence` EQUALS NOTHING
-- no offence committed: the "If" is unmet
#ASSERT `form 6.2 if the person commits an offence under subsection 145(3), the Form states that` FALSE `forms 6 to 11.1 a warrant for the arrest of the person may be issued` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no offence committed: JUST FALSE whatever the consequence asked
#ASSERT `form 6.2 if the person commits an offence under subsection 145(3), the Form states that` FALSE `forms 6 to 11.1 another consequence` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- on interim release and does not comply
#ASSERT `form 6.2 the summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order to which the person is subject may be cancelled` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- on interim release and is charged with an offence after the summons was issued
#ASSERT `form 6.2 the summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order to which the person is subject may be cancelled` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- on interim release but neither limb
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `form 6.2 the summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order to which the person is subject may be cancelled` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the name is a "may" that gives a power or liberty and its "If" gate is unmet; the text limits the grant in its own wording and is silent outside the limit, so the answer is NOTHING, not a "may not" (name-test sweep, fork F-W; the other reading, a failed "If" as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE).
#ASSERT `form 6.2 the summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order to which the person is subject may be cancelled` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not on interim release: "If you are on interim release" is unmet
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `form 6.2 the summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order to which the person is subject may be cancelled` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the name is a "may" that gives a power or liberty and its "If" gate is unmet; the text limits the grant in its own wording and is silent outside the limit, so the answer is NOTHING, not a "may not" (name-test sweep, fork F-W; the other reading, a failed "If" as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE).
#ASSERT `form 6.2 the summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order to which the person is subject may be cancelled` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not on interim release, both limbs
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `form 6.2 the summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order to which the person is subject may be cancelled` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the name is a "may" that gives a power or liberty and its "If" gate is unmet; the text limits the grant in its own wording and is silent outside the limit, so the answer is NOTHING, not a "may not" (name-test sweep, fork F-W; the other reading, a failed "If" as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE).
#ASSERT `form 6.2 the summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order to which the person is subject may be cancelled` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "as a result, you may be detained in custody"
#ASSERT `form 6.2 the person may be detained in custody as a result of the cancellation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not cancelled
#ASSERT `form 6.2 the person may be detained in custody as a result of the cancellation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Form 6.2: 10 days until the day set out. Expected from the text: attending at day 5 -> FULFILLED; attending at day 10 (the last day) -> FULFILLED; never attending by day 11 -> BREACH.
#TRACE `form 6.2 the person must appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `form 6.2 appears for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` AT 5

#TRACE `form 6.2 the person must appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `form 6.2 appears for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` AT 10

#TRACE `form 6.2 the person must appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` 10 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 11

