§ `Tests -- Form 9, the appearance notice`

-- charges laid, failed to appear or attend, no lawful excuse
#ASSERT `form 9 item 6(a) warning: where charges have been laid, unless the person has a lawful excuse, failing to appear or to attend court is an offence under subsection 145(3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "in the case where charges have been laid" is unmet
#ASSERT `form 9 item 6(a) warning: where charges have been laid, unless the person has a lawful excuse, failing to appear or to attend court is an offence under subsection 145(3)` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "unless you have a lawful excuse"
#ASSERT `form 9 item 6(a) warning: where charges have been laid, unless the person has a lawful excuse, failing to appear or to attend court is an offence under subsection 145(3)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "if you fail to appear ... or to attend court" is unmet
#ASSERT `form 9 item 6(a) warning: where charges have been laid, unless the person has a lawful excuse, failing to appear or to attend court is an offence under subsection 145(3)` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no charges laid and fails to appear at the judicial referral hearing
#ASSERT `form 9 item 6(b) warning: charges may be laid against the person for the alleged offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no charges laid, but appeared at the hearing
#ASSERT `form 9 item 6(b) warning: charges may be laid against the person for the alleged offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- charges have been laid: "in the case where no charges have been laid" is unmet
#ASSERT `form 9 item 6(b) warning: charges may be laid against the person for the alleged offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- charges laid and no failure
#ASSERT `form 9 item 6(b) warning: charges may be laid against the person for the alleged offence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- committed the offence: a warrant for arrest may be issued
#ASSERT `form 9 if the person commits an offence under subsection 145(3), the Form states that` TRUE `forms 6 to 11.1 a warrant for the arrest of the person may be issued` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- ... and the person may be liable to a fine
#ASSERT `form 9 if the person commits an offence under subsection 145(3), the Form states that` TRUE `forms 6 to 11.1 the person may be liable to a fine` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- ... or to imprisonment
#ASSERT `form 9 if the person commits an offence under subsection 145(3), the Form states that` TRUE `forms 6 to 11.1 the person may be liable to imprisonment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- ... or to both
#ASSERT `form 9 if the person commits an offence under subsection 145(3), the Form states that` TRUE `forms 6 to 11.1 the person may be liable to both a fine and imprisonment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a consequence the sentence does not name: not covered
#ASSERT `form 9 if the person commits an offence under subsection 145(3), the Form states that` TRUE `forms 6 to 11.1 another consequence` EQUALS NOTHING
-- no offence committed: the "If" is unmet
#ASSERT `form 9 if the person commits an offence under subsection 145(3), the Form states that` FALSE `forms 6 to 11.1 a warrant for the arrest of the person may be issued` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no offence committed: JUST FALSE whatever the consequence asked
#ASSERT `form 9 if the person commits an offence under subsection 145(3), the Form states that` FALSE `forms 6 to 11.1 another consequence` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "It is not a lawful excuse": an inaccurate description of the offence
#ASSERT `form 9 the inaccuracy of the description is a lawful excuse to an offence under subsection 145(3)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- any other ground of excuse is not addressed by the sentence
#ASSERT `form 9 the inaccuracy of the description is a lawful excuse to an offence under subsection 145(3)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- does not comply
#ASSERT `form 9 the appearance notice may be cancelled` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- is charged with committing an offence after
#ASSERT `form 9 the appearance notice may be cancelled` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- both limbs
#ASSERT `form 9 the appearance notice may be cancelled` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- neither limb: the "If" is unmet
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `form 9 the appearance notice may be cancelled` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the name is a "may" that gives a power or liberty and its "If" gate is unmet; the text limits the grant in its own wording and is silent outside the limit, so the answer is NOTHING, not a "may not" (name-test sweep, fork F-W; the other reading, a failed "If" as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE).
#ASSERT `form 9 the appearance notice may be cancelled` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "as a result, you may be detained in custody", once cancelled
#ASSERT `form 9 the person may be detained in custody as a result of the cancellation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not cancelled: the result clause does not apply
#ASSERT `form 9 the person may be detained in custody as a result of the cancellation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Form 9 item 4: 30 days until the day set out. Expected from the text: attending at day 12 -> FULFILLED; attending at day 30 (the last day) -> FULFILLED; never attending by day 31 -> BREACH.
#TRACE `form 9 the accused must attend court` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `form 9 attends court as required` AT 12

#TRACE `form 9 the accused must attend court` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `form 9 attends court as required` AT 30

#TRACE `form 9 the accused must attend court` 30 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 31

§ `Tests -- Form 10, the undertaking`

-- Form 10 item 4, the mandatory condition: 30 days until the day set out. Expected from the text: attending at day 12 -> FULFILLED; attending at day 30 (the last day) -> FULFILLED; never attending by day 31 -> BREACH.
#TRACE `form 10 the accused must attend court` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `form 10 attends court as required` AT 12

#TRACE `form 10 the accused must attend court` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `form 10 attends court as required` AT 30

#TRACE `form 10 the accused must attend court` 30 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 31

-- a condition indicated by a check mark
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 the person must comply with the condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a condition not indicated by a check mark: outside the sentence
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 the person must comply with the condition` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- reasonable, and necessary to ensure attendance in court
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 a condition may be checked` TRUE `form 10 to ensure the accused's attendance in court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- reasonable, and necessary for the safety and security of a victim
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 a condition may be checked` TRUE `form 10 to ensure the safety and security of a victim of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- reasonable, and necessary for the safety and security of a witness
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 a condition may be checked` TRUE `form 10 to ensure the safety and security of a witness to the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- reasonable, and necessary to prevent continuation or repetition
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 a condition may be checked` TRUE `form 10 to prevent the continuation or repetition of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- reasonable, and necessary to prevent another offence
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 a condition may be checked` TRUE `form 10 to prevent the commission of another offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- reasonable but not necessary for any of the five purposes: "check only those that are ... necessary"
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 a condition may be checked` TRUE `form 10 none of those purposes` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- necessary but not reasonable in the circumstances of the offence: "check only those that are reasonable"
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 a condition may be checked` FALSE `form 10 to ensure the accused's attendance in court` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- neither
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 a condition may be checked` FALSE `form 10 none of those purposes` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a firearm: named in paragraph (i)
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must not possess the thing` `forms 10 and 11 a firearm` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a cross-bow: named in paragraph (i)
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must not possess the thing` `forms 10 and 11 a cross-bow` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a prohibited weapon: named in paragraph (i)
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must not possess the thing` `forms 10 and 11 a prohibited weapon` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a restricted weapon: named in paragraph (i)
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must not possess the thing` `forms 10 and 11 a restricted weapon` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a prohibited device: named in paragraph (i)
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must not possess the thing` `forms 10 and 11 a prohibited device` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a firearm part: named in paragraph (i)
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must not possess the thing` `forms 10 and 11 a firearm part` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- ammunition: named in paragraph (i)
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must not possess the thing` `forms 10 and 11 ammunition` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- prohibited ammunition: named in paragraph (i)
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must not possess the thing` `forms 10 and 11 prohibited ammunition` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an explosive substance: named in paragraph (i)
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must not possess the thing` `forms 10 and 11 an explosive substance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the document is to be surrendered, not described as something the person must not possess
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must not possess the thing` `forms 10 and 11 an authorization, licence or registration certificate or other document enabling the acquisition or possession of a firearm` EQUALS NOTHING
-- a thing the list does not name: not covered (the list is not closed)
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must not possess the thing` `forms 10 and 11 something else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- a named thing in the person's possession
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must surrender the thing` `forms 10 and 11 a firearm` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "those that are in your possession": not in possession
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must surrender the thing` `forms 10 and 11 a firearm` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "and also any authorization, licence or registration certificate or other document"
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must surrender the thing` `forms 10 and 11 an authorization, licence or registration certificate or other document enabling the acquisition or possession of a firearm` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the document is not in the person's possession
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must surrender the thing` `forms 10 and 11 an authorization, licence or registration certificate or other document enabling the acquisition or possession of a firearm` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a thing the sentence names
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must surrender the thing` `forms 10 and 11 something else` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not in possession
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must surrender the thing` `forms 10 and 11 something else` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(not more than $500)": the limit itself
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (j) the amount the person may be required to promise to pay is within the limit` 500 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- below the limit
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (j) the amount the person may be required to promise to pay is within the limit` 499 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- zero is not more than $500
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (j) the amount the person may be required to promise to pay is within the limit` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- one cent over the limit
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (j) the amount the person may be required to promise to pay is within the limit` 500.01 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- over the limit
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (j) the amount the person may be required to promise to pay is within the limit` 501 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not ordinarily resident in the province, amount at the limit
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (k) the person may be required to make the deposit` 500 FALSE 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- resident, but does not reside within 200 km (201 km)
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (k) the person may be required to make the deposit` 300 TRUE 201 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- resident and resides within 200 km (exactly 200): outside the ground
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (k) the person may be required to make the deposit` 300 TRUE 200 EQUALS NOTHING
-- resident and within 200 km
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (k) the person may be required to make the deposit` 300 TRUE 100 EQUALS NOTHING
-- over the $500 limit, though the ground is met
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (k) the person may be required to make the deposit` 501 FALSE 500 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- over the limit and outside the ground: the limit answers first
#ASSERT `form 10 item 5 paragraph (k) the person may be required to make the deposit` 501 TRUE 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- both consent in writing
#ASSERT `form 10 item 7 the conditions may be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor and the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the person has not consented: outside this route
#ASSERT `form 10 item 7 the conditions may be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor and the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the prosecutor has not consented: outside this route
#ASSERT `form 10 item 7 the conditions may be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor and the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "you or the prosecutor may apply to a justice of the peace"
#ASSERT `form 10 item 7 the applicant may apply to a justice of the peace to replace the undertaking with a release order under section 515` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- someone else: not named
#ASSERT `form 10 item 7 the applicant may apply to a justice of the peace to replace the undertaking with a release order under section 515` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "you or the prosecutor may apply to a justice of the peace"
#ASSERT `form 10 item 7 the applicant may apply to a justice of the peace to vary the undertaking` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- someone else: not named
#ASSERT `form 10 item 7 the applicant may apply to a justice of the peace to vary the undertaking` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not yet cancelled, changed, discharged, sentenced or detained
#ASSERT `form 10 the conditions remain in effect` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "until they are cancelled or changed"
#ASSERT `form 10 the conditions remain in effect` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "until you have been discharged, sentenced or otherwise detained by the court"
#ASSERT `form 10 the conditions remain in effect` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- both
#ASSERT `form 10 the conditions remain in effect` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- failed to follow a condition, no lawful excuse
#ASSERT `form 10 warning: unless the person has a lawful excuse, failing to follow any of the conditions is an offence under section 145` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "unless you have a lawful excuse"
#ASSERT `form 10 warning: unless the person has a lawful excuse, failing to follow any of the conditions is an offence under section 145` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no failure: the "if you fail" is unmet
#ASSERT `form 10 warning: unless the person has a lawful excuse, failing to follow any of the conditions is an offence under section 145` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no failure and an excuse
#ASSERT `form 10 warning: unless the person has a lawful excuse, failing to follow any of the conditions is an offence under section 145` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- committed the offence: a warrant for arrest may be issued
#ASSERT `form 10 if the person commits an offence under section 145, the Form states that` TRUE `forms 6 to 11.1 a warrant for the arrest of the person may be issued` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- ... and the person may be liable to a fine
